{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar","id":399276,"title":"Happy Moonday! Here, have a Lunar!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T14:03:52-08:00","id":399276,"title":"Happy Moonday! Here, have a Lunar!","content":"<b>SOROL SANDSWIMMER</b><br /> <br /> Sorol began life as every other Dune Person, growing up in underground caves, learning the legends of his people from manskin tapestries, and eager to prove himself to his close-knit community. On his 17th birthday, Sorol set out on his adult rite of passage, a quest to hunt and kill a human being, render them down and bring back their thighbone as his own personal sleeping bone, marking him as a full adult member of the tribe. <br /> <br /> Things did not go as expected. Sorol soon found himself the hunted one, and captured by a caravan of Guild slavers. They laughed as they tied him to their wagons, and showed no mercy as the relentless sun seared his uncovered flesh. One or two days of such treatment should have been enough to finish him off, but Sorol hung on through the pain, promising himself that he would survive this. On the fifth day, as the pitiless sun sank, and the desert cooled, he lay in agony, until distracted by the capering antics of a tiny silver mouse caught in a complicated rope. Sorol spoke words of camaderie to the rodent, praising its never-ending struggles until it finally freed itself. On a whim, he imitated its movements, suddenly finding the pain recede somewhat from his now-fluid limbs. Shrugging off the ropes, Sorol instinctively dove into the ground as though it were water, easily escaping the Guild. <br /> <br /> Exhausted and agonized, Sorol made it back to his tribe, presenting himself to his elders. The oldest shamans were quickly called and consulted. On the one hand, he had clearly failed his quest for adulthood. On the other, he had been touched by Luna herself. But why had the Changing Lady blessed him with so...questionable a form? For the Spirit Shape Sorol had been gifted with was that of an Eight-Tailed Mole Hound, the ancient hunters of tribes of the sand!<br /> <br /> After consulting with the spirits, the shamans gave their verdict: Sorol would have to complete his quest, but the bone of a human would no longer suffice. Instead, he would have to find the bone of a suitably challenging target, appropriate to his new status. Bidding goodbye to his family, Sorol once again set out...<br /> <br /> For half a year he traveled, exploring his new powers and the lands of the South. Soon, he was discovered by the Lunar elder Ka-Koshu, who identified Sorol as the reincarnation of his recently deceased companion Namiha Featherback. Ka-Koshu explained the basics of being Chosen by Luna to Sorol, put him through the Trials, fixing his Caste with Moonsilver tattooing, and bestowed upon him the deed-name of Sandswimmer. Before he sent Sorol on, he warned him that his destiny could well take him beyond the confines of his people.<br /> <br /> Since then, Sorol Sandswimmer has ranged across the southern deserts, attacking Guild caravans, fighting desert basilisks, running with furnace rhinos, debating with Ash Devourers, and communing with the desert spirits. One incident lingers in his mind, where he drove off a pride of fae Lion-Folk. He was simply attacking the Raksha, but was unprepared for the cheers and applause from the human settlement they were attacking. Sorol has since used the many animal forms he has acquired to sneak into human camps to observe them closely. <br /> <br /> These observations are confirming Ka-Koshu's teachings and his own hazy memories of the First Age: That humans are not so different from his people after all, and that both share a common heritage; but can his people be made to accept that? For now, he seeks a human fit to perform the Sacred Hunt upon, that he may walk among them as one of their own, an experience he hopes will determine his future course. <br /> <br /> Sandswimmer still must become a legal adult of the tribe before they will listen to him, of course. He has heard increasing tales of humans Chosen like himself, only by the hateful sun. If he could bring one of their bones back to his people, that may be enough of an accomplish to unify all the tribes of sand behind him...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Sorol Sandswimmer is a newly Exalted Changing Moon, with the Spirit Shape of an Eight-Tailed Mole Hound. His albinism has become his Tell, with his Mole Hound and Hound Man True Forms having stark white fur and pink eyes. He has learned Stamina charms that enable him to withstand the bright light of day without harm, but he still avoids it as he finds it uncomfortable. <br /> <br /> He does not know that Eternal Crimson Sunset, the Solar who created his people in the First Age, has reincarnated as one of his people, a Malefactor who uses her wiles to subvert their people to the will of the Yozis. If Sorol learns this, he will stop at nothing to claim her for his sleeping bone. Unless she turns out to be his spiritual mate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:10:44-08:00","id":399311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar#post399276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He does not know that Eternal Crimson Sunset, the Solar who created his people in the First Age, has reincarnated as one of his people, a Malefactor who uses her wiles to subvert their people to the will of the Yozis. If Sorol learns this, he will stop at nothing to claim her for his sleeping bone. Unless she turns out to be his spiritual mate...</div> </div> </div> </div>This would stop him from getting his murder on... why exactly? From what you've written of Sorol, he isn't the type to regard the Solar/Lunar bond with a great deal of spiritual reverence. Given how you've described him, it seems discovering his bond was with someone that heinous would make him more likely to move straight to disemboweling, not less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 02-09-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:26:17-08:00","id":399353,"title":"","content":"Well, it would depend on how strong the Bond was. I was kind of assuming a 5, although that doesn't have to be automatic, I admit. <br /> <br /> Of course, if we go with Dean Shomshak's Bond Revision, then it could well compel him to kill her!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:28:22-08:00","id":399355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=399353#post399353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it would depend on how strong the Bond was. I was kind of assuming a 5, although that doesn't have to be automatic, I admit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignore terrible bond mechanics in general. Or at least ignore the parts that stand in the way of proper expressions of the character's personality.<br /> <br /> Bond 5 certainly does not have to mean &quot;I am compelled to not kill you and am actually your widdle puppy slave.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:39:24-08:00","id":399368,"title":"","content":"Are sleeping bones an actual thing from the books or something you made up to expand the culture of the people that your character is part of?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I like it. I wouldn't personally have the bond make a difference, but I can see why someone might want to in service of the story they want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:40:45-08:00","id":399369,"title":"","content":"&quot;Now I extra have to kill you, capture your Exaltation, give it to Lytek, get the vitriol and brass scrapped off and make sure it goes to where it's supposed to go.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:42:23-08:00","id":399374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=399368#post399368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are sleeping bones an actual thing from the books or something you made up to expand the culture of the people that your character is part of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dune People sleep under the sand during the day and basically use hollowed-out bones as snorkels to breathe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:47:52-08:00","id":399382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=399311#post399311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would stop him from getting his murder on... why exactly? From what you've written of Sorol, he isn't the type to regard the Solar/Lunar bond with a great deal of spiritual reverence. Given how you've described him, it seems discovering his bond was with someone that heinous would make him more likely to move straight to disemboweling, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Solar Lunar bond can be about strong emotions. Don't have to be positive. Love and hate are two sides of the same coin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:50:21-08:00","id":399537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=399355#post399355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignore terrible bond mechanics in general. Or at least ignore the parts that stand in the way of proper expressions of the character's personality.<br /> <br /> Bond 5 certainly does not have to mean &quot;I am compelled to not kill you and am actually your widdle puppy slave.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This, yes. It can be a bond of hatred as easily as love, and even a bond of love doesn't compel the Lunar to rewrite their personality at the Solar's (Infernal's) whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:21:30-08:00","id":400972,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was going by RAW, where Solar Bond 2 is that you find their influence hard to resist, and 3 is that you can hardly resist being their best friend or lover &quot;even if you hate them&quot;! I know, I know, &quot;please don't feed the bad mechanics&quot;, but, as Mizu pointed out, if I was going to bring this up in an actual story, it would be in the service of complicating Sorol's goals.<br /> <br /> Is there anything in canon that says Lunars view their Solar mates primarily as their past selves, such that they would want to kill an Infernal/Abyssal to free their past mate from their now-tainted nature? I get the impression they see them as their current incarnations and take them on their own terms, first and foremost, aside from elders like Lilith, who personally knew the previous incarnation. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on any other complications or challenges Sandswimmer might face in his newly exalted life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:30:33-08:00","id":400981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=400972#post400972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything in canon that says Lunars view their Solar mates primarily as their past selves, such that they would want to kill an Infernal/Abyssal to free their past mate from their now-tainted nature? I get the impression they see them as their current incarnations and take them on their own terms, first and foremost, aside from elders like Lilith, who personally knew the previous incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there's nothing in canon that says this. <br /> <br /> The only way a Lunar would really know is if they were a First Age survivor and remembered their Mate as being a Solar not this....polluted green or black <i>thing.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:04:47-08:00","id":425432,"title":"","content":"<b>IT</b> no longer remembers the name it was born with, or much of anything else about its mortal life; occasional flashes of family life, villagers on fire, running through the woods, surviving on whatever it offered. There was a shining silver deer keeping it company in those days...or perhaps it was an owl...or maybe a young boy, it remembers its companion differently sometimes. She told it many things, singing words and stories which it often wishes it could remember. But it remembers the lessons well enough, how to hunt and take on the skin of crawling and flying things, so that it could crawl and fly itself.<br /> <br /> Then, the Burning Men came. Well, some of them burned, others threw lightening and rocks. It fled again, this time into lands as fluid and changing as its own skin could be. It stayed there, perhaps too long, for soon it found itself changing without meaning to. Keeping a stable form took real effort, especially after the storms of strangeness ripped its own shadow away from it. It wept, and chased after the laughing shade, but wasn't fast enough. Shortly after, it changed so much that it couldn't even recall what it had originally looked like. And the hunger grew, and wasn't satisfied by the little animals anymore...<br /> <br /> The Laughing Hunters came soon after. It fled again, but this time, was angry, and so hid, tracked them and took them by surprise, running them down and ripping their shimmering hearts out to feast upon. So nourishing, those hearts, even if they gave strange dreams. Soon after, another one found it, but this one was beautiful and kind, not unlike the Silver Friend it barely remembered. She sang to it, whispered and stroked it, and gave it gifts. In time, it was utterly charmed. With its permission, she reached deep into it and pulled forth its Love, which she cunningly fashioned into a shining silver necklace, that she looped around its neck. Then, she pulled forth its Restraint, and with a theatrical flourish, turned it into a voluminous cloak to wrap around its shifting body. Then she told it where it could find its shadow, back in the still, quiet places, and sent it on its way...<br /> <br /> It now returns to the fixed lands, marveling at how much things there <i>don't</i> change, and at how much clearer its own head seems. The hunger still remains and grows greater still, but it has found the means to quell it for a time. Yes, there will be no more running now, only hunting; its own shadow and anything else that gets in its way...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> It is close to full Chimera-hood, if not there already. It possesses whatever random Mutations the ST feels it needs, the Amnesia and Phobia (butterflies) Derangements, and has the access to the shifting Caste powers that all Casteless enjoy. It has had its Compassion and Temperance Virtues forged into Grace Artifacts by a Raksha Noble; the delicate-looking silver chain-collar gives her some control over it, while the cloak helps magically conceal its mutated nature until it is too late for its victims. This process seems to have cured its insanity, somewhat, making it more capable of clear and complex thought, speech and action than the average Chimera.<br /> <br /> The Wyld sliced away its capability to cast a shadow and gave its old shadow independence and awareness; its shadows' true whereabouts and activities are up to the ST. It has a powerful Intimacy to regaining this shadow and will do much to further this. If it succeeds, then it may also regain many of its memories and even its name...<br /> <br /> (I wrote this right after having the idea, without consulting the rules, so feel free to tell me what doesn't work, and/or how it can!)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:01:37-08:00","id":425650,"title":"","content":"Did they get rid of Wyld mutants not being able to Exalt in 2nd edition? Because back in my day, the rules didn't let me Exalt a mutie, although they'd let me mutate an Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:28:50-08:00","id":425673,"title":"","content":"I always interpreted the bond in that the characters Exalted Essence holds the memory of a past relationship that was so strong that the emotions behind that relationship are carried on from one exaltation to another. This could be star crossed lovers, inseparable best friends or an unrelenting enmity. Generally these bonds were forged by the extremely long associations during the First Age (and typically between Lunars and Solars because of the mate association) but i do not limit them to such. I allow Solar/Solar bonds and Lunar/Lunar bonds and even Bonds with Sidereals, though those would be ultra rare because of how fucking snooty the Siddies tend to be. This way I can have Solars bonded to Abyssals and let the fun commence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:58:06-08:00","id":426176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=425650#post425650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they get rid of Wyld mutants not being able to Exalt in 2nd edition? Because back in my day, the rules didn't let me Exalt a mutie, although they'd let me mutate an Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only if the Wyld Mutant is so mutated that their soul no longer counts as human, like the Singers of the Deep, who are now a separate species from humanity. But a few Mutations wouldn't be enough to prevent Exaltation by themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:39:52-08:00","id":426218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=426176#post426176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Only if the Wyld Mutant is so mutated that their soul no longer counts as human, like the Singers of the Deep, who are now a separate species from humanity. But a few Mutations wouldn't be enough to prevent Exaltation by themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 1e wouldn't have had explicit rules for mutant Exalted if they weren't allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T05:31:45-08:00","id":426467,"title":"","content":"Hand-of-Omega have you got a collection of all the characters you've written up of late?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:31:27-08:00","id":426690,"title":"","content":"Nope. Some are ideas that have been knocking around my head for awhile, but others just come to me a couple of hours before posting, like that last one. Sometimes, ideas in the writeup just occur to me as I'm writing them, like the Sidereal who uses NRS to relocate his bar to various districts of Nexus (I really like that one)! <br /> <br /> Hope you're enjoying them so far...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T06:36:47-08:00","id":427663,"title":"","content":"Very much so! They are all getting added to my big old book of NPCs to drop into games at some point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T06:48:15-08:00","id":427668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=425432#post425432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>IT</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Now I have to stat Pennywise as a Spider-Totem Lunar. Clown-Totem Lunar?? Clown-Spider-Totem Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:33:01-08:00","id":428655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very much so! They are all getting added to my big old book of NPCs to drop into games at some point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Good to know these ideas will live on and find good use!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=427668#post427668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I have to stat Pennywise as a Spider-Totem Lunar. Clown-Totem Lunar?? Clown-Spider-Totem Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...I guess I didn't need to ever sleep again anyway.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 03-05-2015, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T00:15:10-08:00","id":428793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=428655#post428655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...I guess I didn't need to ever sleep again anyway.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For your sake, I'll try and make it a little more light-hearted than the source material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:20:57-07:00","id":434243,"title":"","content":"<b>ALIYAH the SAND WITCH</b><br /> <br /> Occasionally, a rare child is born into the Jackal Tribes with none of their diseases or deformities, and manages to survive to adulthood. Woe unto them, for their lot is a hard one, as they are resented for their unblemished bodies, and given most of the hardest work, and the least of what little the tribe has. Aliyah was one such child, and stoically took her burden as she was taught to. As she grew taller and more beautiful, however, she incited more jealousy, as well as resentment, and some sought to mar her blossoming beauty permanently. They secretly made offerings to the Gods of disease that they worshiped to strike her with all their ailments, that she may be even more disfigured than most, if she survived at all.<br /> <br /> This the gods did, and as the poor girl swam in the delirium of her maladies, she beheld a silver light, sometimes a butterfly, a vulture, or a hyena, but always laughing, just out of reach. As Aliyah finally caught it, her fever broke and the diseases fled before the silver radiance bursting from her. The shaman trying to cure her and the women glorying in her death all stood amazed, and fell prostrate before this miracle...<br /> <br /> In the time since, Aliyah has redefined her position in her tribe. She realizes that she does not yet have the wisdom to rule it, and so is content to learn from the God-Blooded shaman who does, and who has explained to her what she is. The others all give her much more respect now, and are just as fearful of her. As for those bitches who condemned her...she does nothing to them. This is not mercy. She knows that she could rend them apart or set spirits upon them to drive them to madness...and they know this, too. Instead, she simply smiles at them, and lets them wait for her eventual vengence. After all, there is nothing they can do now, and in a way, she owes them for her new elevated status. And even if she never moves against them, they must still live out the rest of their lives being themselves, which is the worst possible revenge...<br /> <br /> Aliyah knows that there are others out there like herself, but has not seen them. As she finishes learning all that her Shaman can teach her of thaumaturgy and the ways of the spirits, she considers leaving her nomadic group, and seeking them out. Or perhaps she should instead seek the truth of the legends of the Jackal Prophet she has always wondered about...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Aliyah is a very young Lunar, currently Casteless, and has little in the way of Backgrounds, besides Mentor, growing Influence and a few Contacts among the spirits. Her aptitude with learning Thaumaturgy and interest in Sorcery suggest she would make a good No-Moon, but other Castes can also specialize in the greater magics. Her Spirit Shape is, fittingly, that of a jackal, and her Tell is a body-wide network of white plague-scars blemishing her otherwise flawless dark skin. Her leading Virtue is Compassion, and her Virtue Flaw is the Curse of the Whipped Dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 03-09-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:49:23-07:00","id":434335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=434243#post434243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SAND WITCH</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jackel </div> </div> </div>Jackal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> she incited more jealously </div> </div> </div>Jealousy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The others all give her much more respect now, as well as fear. </div> </div> </div>They give her fear? Does this mean they're afraid of her, or they make her afraid of them? My guess would be the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for those bitches who condemned her\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Language, Hand! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After all, there is nothing they can do now\u2026 </div> </div> </div>They could stab her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly the wording of this bit feels a little too mortals-don't-matter, but maybe I'm looking at it too hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jackel </div> </div> </div>Jackal! Jackal! It's a jackal! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aliyah\u2026 has little in the way of Backgrounds, besides Mentor. </div> </div> </div>No Influence? No Resources or Followers? Besides, you gotta spend those dots on <i>something</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> jackel </div> </div> </div>One more for the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:21:45-07:00","id":434392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=434335#post434335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yum.<br /> <br /> Jackal?<br /> <br /> Jealousy?<br /> <br /> They give her fear? Does this mean they're afraid of her, or they make her afraid of them? My guess would be the former.<br /> <br /> Language, Hand!<br /> <br /> They could stab her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly the wording of this bit feels a little too mortals-don't-matter, but maybe I'm looking at it too hard.<br /> <br /> Jackal! Jackal! It's a jackal! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No Influence? No Resources or Followers? Besides, you gotta spend those dots on <i>something</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One more for the road.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She's not completely invulnerable to being stabbed or something by those bitches (I stand by that term, in this instance!), but they're young women basically paralyzed by religious terror, so they'd never take the chance, so long as she's not overtly threatening them. They're hoping she'll just forget about them...<br /> <br /> All other criticisms noted and implemented. Thanks!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:18:37-07:00","id":589225,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LEVIATHAN</b></div> The island nation of Coral is well-known the world over for its cutting edge electronics and entertainments, as well as for its distinctive clash of ancient pagodas side-by-side with towering neon skyscrapers. But the ancient pride of the people still bears a deep scar, seared into its national psyche by the nuclear fire of defeat. None symbolize both this pride and its wound as well as The Admiral.<br /> <br /> Leviathan was a direct descendant of Coral's class of famed warrior-aristocrats, the Invincibles, and always carried himself with dignity and honor throughout his naval career. Although he warned his superiors against declaring war on Meruvia with a surprise first strike, once the order was given, he carried it out to the best of his ability, and fought on all through the war, until his government finally capitulated. He stoically endured the following humiliations, of having the Sea Lord publicly abdicate if favor of a mere Prime Minister, of having the centuries-long tradition of the Invincibles formally dissolved, and being unable to legally carry their ancestral weapons in public, of being denied any military except for a pathetic, symbolic &quot;self-defense force&quot;. <br /> <br /> Leviathan could have endured all this, but it was seeing his people, or the young among them at least, seemingly eager to throw away their ancient culture to embrace the clothing, speech and ways of their conquerors that finally moved him to act. Gathering a group of like-minded old soldiers and officials, he masterminded the takeover of a military outpost on the coast. Reading prepared statements to the world media, they explained that this act was an act of defiance to the present state of affairs in their land, one they hoped would wake up their people; and so, they committed ritual suicide, in the old fashion, which ended with tossing themselves into the sea. <br /> <br /> As the sharks came for his bleeding body, Leviathan decided that he might as well fight them for it...and shocked himself by winning! The silvery glow illuminating the depths around him had something to do with it, as he had now become one of the Lunar Exalted the world whispered about in its legends and tall-tales.<br /> <br /> It didn't take long for Leviathan to master his new state, and he soon realized that his service to his people, disappointed as he was in them, was still not over. A legacy of Meruvian nuclear bombing had been to create a Wyld Zone near Coral, which had been mutating the sea life there. Now, massive crazed behemoths began emerging from the sea and rampaging across Coral, and even the occupation army couldn't stop them (without even more nuclear bombing, which would be counterproductive). Assuming his massive warform, Leviathan stepped forward onto Coral soil once more, which he promised himself to do only in defense of it, and slew the invaders of his homeland.<br /> <br /> Although he has not taken on his original form since then, somehow the people could tell it was him; perhaps it was in his soulful eyes, or possibly it was just a whimsical belief which spread and stuck, but people began saying that the spirit of the Admiral had fallen into the sea, mutated in the Wyld waters, and came back when he was needed the most. He never tarries after destroying his enemies, and never moves against Meruvian forces unless they attack him first; if Meruvian-style buildings happen to get crushed during his fights more often than not, however, few comment on it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T07:52:04-07:00","id":590202,"title":"","content":"If I ever run a modern shard, the above is 100% canon. Lunar-zilla... that is so awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Murcushio: Sure, you avoid all that messy withdrawal, but you still need to <i>stop doing heroin</i> (for the purposes of this discussion your cousin is named Heroin).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4657-maxastro","name":"MaxAstro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:29:52-07:00","id":590770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaxAstro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=590202#post590202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I ever run a modern shard, the above is 100% canon. Lunar-zilla... that is so awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, glad you can use him. And he's Godzilla, by way of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukio_Mishima#Coup_attempt_and_ritual_suicide\" target=\"_blank\">Mishima!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T20:57:05-07:00","id":690826,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>TYR</b></div> <br /> Tyr was a native-born Haslanti, raised in Icehome, from which he joined the Fyrd, eventually graduating into the elite commando division of the Ears of the North, the Blooded Hawks. Unlike many of his ferocious compatriots, he found the time to divide his life between this duty and a well-balanced home life, marrying the love of his life and raising a family with her, stationed in one of the League's largest iceholt barges, a virtual village in a boat, parked on the far Great Ice of the frozen White Sea. <br /> <br /> After a mission, Tyr and his comrades returned to find the iceholt mysteriously gone, with no tracks in ice or snow. A quick divining revealed that it had been swallowed by a rare bank of Wyldfog, which instantly transported it further into the North. As time was of the essence, the small band of Blooded Hawks readied themselves, and marched to the rescue of their people, armed and armored against the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, they ran into something worse: the shambling dead, in the process of being taken over by a Deathknight. She slew Tyr's fellows one by one, reanimating them to join her army. Tyr fought long and hard, so much so that when he was finally overpowered by the husks of his teammates, she mockingly told him that he had earned her respect, so that she wouldn't kill him on the spot or reanimate his corpse. Instead, she had him crucified with daggers upon a boulder, and left him there, her derisive laughter faded with the howling wind, that carried the scent of his blood to any predators in the darkening evening. And then the Hushed Ones came...<br /> <br /> After pulling himself down off the boulder, slaughtering the Hushed Ones and treating his wounds, Tyr considered heading after the Abyssal or going home for reinforcements, but his loyalty to his family was stronger than anything else. And so he set off into the rising snowstorm northward. On the way, he fell into the snowtrap burrowed out by a Snow Lion, which instantly attacked! Its pelt helped keep Tyr warmer and dryer than he had been, just as its meat helped him keep his strength up. <br /> <br /> But as the miles stretched on, the driving wind and snow was almost too much, and he sank to using his hands to drag himself on through the snow, never stopping, never slowing...Tyr didn't even notice when the whipping wind whisked the pelt off of him, because now he had an almost identical one of his own. He could suddenly see with the help of the silvery radiance lighting up the snow around him, snow which no long froze and hurt his paw-like hands as he effortlessly pulled himself through the snow, driven by a primal hunger of the hunt, somehow catching the scents of his home and family, nearer than he had hoped for!<br /> <br /> Tyr found the iceholt, his newly-sharpened senses easily putting together the tale of what had happened here; how the Fair Folk had descended upon this ripe morsel, slaying all of the capable defenders, and taking the rest to stock their frosty larders with, that they could slowly feast upon the steaming hot nightmares they would painstaking wring from hot, tortured hearts and souls. <br /> Fortunately, Tyr caught up with them before they reached their Freehold, driving off the Winter Folk and gathering the survivors for the long march home. While not all made it, his wife and children were among those who did. Tyr then presented himself to the Oligarchs, announced his new state, and declared his renewed loyalty to the Haslanti League, if they would but allow him to serve. <br /> <br /> While they deliberated, the Grandmothers, the true power behind the Ears of the North, evaluated Tyr. Unknown even to those wise women, one of their number was Keen-Eyed Snowcat, a Lunar Exalt who monitored the League for the Twisted Stone Pack. She approached Tyr, took his measure, and swayed the others to allow him to stay, albeit as a &quot;special asset&quot; for exceptional missions, not unlike the League's loyal Night Caste Elias Tremalion (Tyr has not yet worked with Elias; he respects his talents and accomplishments, but doesn't think much of the man himself, so far). <br /> <br /> Tyr is now coming to terms with the fact that, at least as far as his fellow Haslanti are concerned, he belongs more to the supernatural world than to their everyday one. Even his closest friends and family cannot hide the superstitious awe they regard him with, and the pain this causes has led him to absent himself from their company more and more. He has become a frequent visitor of the House of Nine Hearths of Emerald and Silver, visiting with the Triads of Ice, Dreams and Fate, and can even be found in Winter Fastness, the castle of Master Winter and Lady Chimney Draft, enjoying their hospitality and listening to their tales of Ages past.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Tyr is a beginning Lunar, with the Spirit Shape of a Snow Lion and the Tell of a white mane (his hair was bright red, but turned white during his Exaltation). Keen-Eyed Snowcat is hisMentor, who introduced him to the Silver Pact and their ways, oversaw his trials that fixed his Caste as a Full Moon, and continues to teach him about the politics of both the League and the Pact, as well as his own nature and duties as Chosen of Luna, and the intricacies of the northern spirit courts. <br /> <br /> Tyr's Backing from the Haslanti League has given him the ability to requisition many supplies, weapons and resources (such as collapsible gliders, crossbows and Feathersteel weapons and armor), giving him a high Arsenal rating. Master Winter has personally created a weapon for him, a Daiklave forged from glowing blue Unmelting Ice, that Tyr has named PermaFang; in addition to having the traits of a Perfect Sword, it inflicts an external penalty of +4 to all creatures vulnerable to cold. <br /> <br /> Tyr is constantly seeking to sharpen his combat skills by sparring with the Gods of the Ennead, as well as with Keen-Eyed Snowcat and her occasional Lunar guests. He is rapidly mastering Lunar Hero Style and other native Combat Charms, and his Mentor may soon see to teaching him other Martial Arts. He looks forward to training with Tremalion, and testing his skills out on the Iron Wolf...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T21:55:07-07:00","id":691990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=426467#post426467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand-of-Omega have you got a collection of all the characters you've written up of late?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chararters are all collected in the lin in my signature :-)<br /> <br /> That was a very nice writeup, Tyr is extremely badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T19:49:33-07:00","id":693354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=691990#post691990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a very nice writeup, Tyr is extremely badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going for a backstory that would make you think, &quot;Oh, this violent incident is how he exalts! Wait, he didn't? Oh, I guess it's this even more over-the-top event...No?! Damn, this guy is hardcore badass way *before* he exalts!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Having said that, I've just had an inspiration for my next Moonchild, and he/she makes Tyr look like a frail grade-schooler!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T11:25:49-07:00","id":698819,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>ORION X. JAEGER</b></div> <br /> There are hundreds of stories throughout the Central Empire that tell of how Commander Jaeger was exalted as a Lunar, each of them more outrageous than the last, yet none of them so implausible as to be untrue. After all, in his hundreds of years serving as a special operative, Jaeger has probably done more to protect the Empire as a whole than any other single individual being. <br /> <br /> It was he (often she, thanks to casual use of the Twin-Faced Hero knack) who exposed the Iselsi Conspiracy to destroy the Thousandth Dynasty, he who rescued the Son of Heaven's many daughters from their ransomed captivity by a Death-Avatar (and then publicly made out with them because <i>he just does not give a fuck!</i>), he who drove off a nightmare horde of Shrieking Ones back into the strange unreality of the Canals, and he who smashed several of the massive terra-forming engines that were attempting to absorb outlying worlds of the Empire into the God-Constellation Autochthon.<br /> <br /> Jaeger isn't a glory-hog, however, and will be the first to give credit to his team, a small unit of humans, aliens and Exalts (including an Alchemical &quot;unplugged&quot; from Autochthon) that crews his Artifact Starship, The Mishaka. While perhaps too eccentric to serve in the regular Legions, their talents and loyalty make them the surrogate family Jaeger lost long ago, and he'd lay down his life for them just as they would for him. <br /> <br /> Most recently, the Mishaka encountered a strange new type of Exalt never recorded before, burning with the green sunlight of the Yozi-Stars. Jaeger reported this to Imperial Center, only to have the massive bureaucracy there unsurprisingly spin its wheels while awaiting more &quot;proof&quot;. Looks like it's time for Jaeger and crew to go back to work again...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Jaeger is a middle-aged Lunar with lots of combat experience, making him one of the foremost warriors in the Known Worlds. He is a Full Moon, with a Honey Badger Spirit Shape, whose Tell is Being the Most Badass Thing Around (or, An Unblinking, Intimidating Gaze/Presence), which also happens to be what his high Reputation represents. Jaeger has War Specialties of Small-Unit Tactics, and Charisma/Manipulation Specialties of Leadership/Intimidation, respectively. He also enjoys the Common Sense and Daredevil Merits, and has many Connections both in the Empire and the Frontier.<br /> <br /> Jaeger has many custom Lunar-Hero Charms, as well as combos with the many supernatural martial arts he has learned, and he has a unique variant of Relentless Lunar Fury that he has developed. He often goes into action with the Beast-Power Concentration knack that allows him to channel his full Lunar powers through his human shape, and his many Stamina Charms make him all but unkillable. <br /> <br /> Jaeger has a high Arsenal rating, giving him access to requisition nearly any Artifact or Equipment he needs for his missions (The Mishaka being regularly stocked with any types of weapons and armor), but he only keeps one Artifact, a Moonsilver Switchklaive that was the first Artifact he ever owned, and is perhaps his oldest Intimacy, besides the Central Empire itself (whose protection forms his Motivation). He once had a powerful Familiar, but he never talks about the mission when he lost it, even though he still has intense Nightmares (as per the Flaw) that indicate that it may still be alive, if no longer what it once was...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:54:26-07:00","id":892239,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>JAEL, THE MOON-MOTHER</b></div> <br /> After finding their way in the world, most Lunars who survive establish a legend for themselves within it. Many are based on mastering the violence and savagery of that world, but some are renown for their boundless compassion for it, instead. Of these, perhaps the most-loved is Jael.<br /> <br /> For the last few hundred years, Jael has been a shining beacon to the Silver Pact of the best the Chosen of Luna can aspire to...although not all agree with the lengths she is willing to go to her nurturing nature. Not only does she treat her fellow Lunars with her healing arts that enable them to recover from injuries and maladies that even their Charms cannot deal with, but she is also known to succor mortals, exalts and spirits of all sorts...even those who are enemies of the Silver Pact and Creation itself!<br /> <br /> These last are meticulously cared for while also being subjected to her soothing manner and incisive questions, all subtly enhanced by the power of Luna. By the time their convalescence is over, many of them have gained a new found appreciation and respect for Creation, some even going out of their way to protect it (or at least lead less harmful lives). <br /> <br /> Jael's moniker of &quot;moon-mother&quot; is not just figurative; she gives her love freely and without prejudice, and has embraced virtually every type of sentient being in Creation, and borne children to many, perhaps more than any other living Moonchild. Most of these creatures, both Beastmen tribes and singular entities, regard Jael as a divine being and give her their utmost love and loyalty, and she could amass a sizable army of her children if she felt the need. <br /> <br /> Jael can take many forms but is most often encountered as a matronly woman of middle years and pleasant cheer, plump and attractive. Her Spirit Shape is a cow, and her Deadly Beastman form a massive bovine woman with a muscular build, snorting nostrils and silver horns. Jael's Tell is a strong smell of milk in her presence, her Limit Trigger is exposing her children or patients to danger, and she most often suffers The Curse of the Mother Hen in Limit Break. <br /> <br /> The Moon-Mother is a Changing Moon, due to her social manner of dealing with problems, but she also has focused heavily on the development of Stamina magic, focusing on endurance, breeding and reproducing drugs and medicines (including Sweet Cordial) with her own biology; these last she often feeds to the sick and injured as sweet milk from her bounteous breasts. Jael enjoys a very high Reputation in the Silver Pact, esp among the Wardens of Gaia, and many Allies and Contacts amongst all sorts of creatures and beings, many of whom owe her Favors.<br /> <br /> Although Jael prefers to avoid combat, she is well-versed in the Art of Victorious Concession, and quite practiced with spells such as the Mists of Eventide, Commanding the Beasts and Summoning of the Harvest. She enhances her healing talents with Artifacts, such as a Satchel of Resplendent Healing, wears a Moonsilver Chainshirt, and can produce a Moonsilver and White Jade Goremaul from Elsewhere, usually to deal with those recalcitrant patients who will not reform their ways before they can inflict more damage upon Creation...<br /> <br /> <i>(This is actually another character I came up with during Mother's Day, but I hesitated to post it because of certain elements that could be seen as silly or juvenile at best, if not outright offensive at worst. But she wouldn't let me go, so I said &quot;screw it&quot;, since it's not like I'm could lose my nonexistent RPG job over fan backlash, and besides, it's in-theme for Exalted's sources, which contain many similar oddities. Still, I feel for the devs/writers who do have to worry about such things..</i>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T21:00:17-07:00","id":892244,"title":"","content":"If necessary, one might imagine she is inspired by <i>Undetale's</i> Goat-Mom Extraordinaire, Toriel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:12:26-07:00","id":892287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=892244#post892244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If necessary, one might imagine she is inspired by <i>Undetale's</i> Goat-Mom Extraordinaire, Toriel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What IS this &quot;Undertale&quot; I keep seeing references to?<br /> <br /> The other inspiration for her, btw, is the Biblical <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jael\" target=\"_blank\">Jael</a>, hammer and all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:58:23-07:00","id":892311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar?p=892287#post892287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What IS this &quot;Undertale&quot; I keep seeing references to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indie game available on Steam for $10.<br /> <br /> Extremely reminiscent of the <i>Earthbound/Mother</i> series on the original Nintendo/Famicon system.<br /> <br /> It will be best for you if you continue to avoid any spoilers for the game, at least until you've seen its trailer and teaser on Steam and decided whether you want to go into it blind or don't mind being spoiled. But seriously, it's just $10 bucks if you're willing to buy it at all.<br /> <br /> Length-wise, it's kind of like <i>Chrono Trigger</i>, with a story that is just long enough, while being short enough to encourage the replayability the game is definitely meant for. It will take more than one pass to get the whole story.<br /> <br /> Also, I appreciate the novelty of a game in which I can win battles without needing to kill anyone or anything... though figuring out how to end or escape a fight without dying or killing gets more and more puzzling. This is, in fact, the true source of the game's &quot;puzzle&quot; genre, more than the obvious &quot;puzzles&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:44:43-07:00","id":892358,"title":"","content":"Well, no longer Moonday, but I've been working on this guy as part of another project. So if I may...<br /> <br /> <b>Regis ap Sora: White Jay of Nightfall</b><br /> <br /> A wandering scholar in a dark leather coat, with long white hair concealed beneath a floppy hat, Regis ap Sora is a genuinely happy man. The pale skinned No Moon has status behind him; he has lived for close on a millennia now, and is one of the Crossroads Society's oldest surviving members. He may be the greatest student of medicine amongst the moon-chosen, and his magic is nothing to sniff at either. By his hand many unblooded Lunars have been brought into the fold, lives have been saved and enemies slain. He has honoured each and every debt he has ever acquired, and the call of a white feathered bird has become a sign of ill luck for Dynasts across the East. There are few Lunars in all of Creation who can match the White Jay's record of commitment to the Silver Pact and its goals.<br /> <br /> And yet, all of this can not erase one simple stain on the No Moon's character. Regis is a necromancer.<br /> <br /> He was so before his Exaltation, at least so he claims. A ghost-blood born upon the isle of Nightfall, it was expected that he pursue the black arts to help defend his nation. Luna chose him to be her herald, necromancy and all, and those spells are useful to a wanderer who relies more on his wits than skill at arms. To the best anyone can determine, ap Sora has made no attempts to contact the Deathlords and does not consider them allies. And yet, if he were to do so, how could even the Silver Pact find out? There is no amount of good that could remove that worry from the minds of elder Lunars, and no amount of reputation that can excuse necromancy to the young, still fearing Thorns and the emergence of the Abyssal Exalted<br /> <br /> Regis ap Sora knows his reputation well, and has stopped trying to fight it. He interacts less with the Pact these days, preferring instead to focus on his own projects and ideas. Many argent eyes, young and old alike, are trained on Regis' growing dominion to the south of Linowan. He has claimed the shadowland known as Ashwater Vale and has brought Tanlin refugees, the tribes of the Llesanti and the ghostly kingdom of Akiden together to found a new kingdom beneath the forest canopy. Regis' expressed hope is that Ashwater will become a civilization in its own right, a safe haven for those who oppose the Realm. The different factions for the moment are held in check by mutual respect for the White Jay, and the construction work is proceeding in accordance with his plans. Those fellow Lunars who are sceptical of ap Sora and his motives are now considering how best to intervene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}